<title>USA: Computer Learning sets 3-for-2 split.</title>
<headline>Computer Learning sets 3-for-2 split.</headline>
<dateline>FAIRFAX, Va. 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Computer Learning Centers Inc said on Monday its board of directors declared a three-for-two stock split.</p>
<p>Distribution will be made on April 14, 1997 to shareholders of record as of the close of business on April 8, 1997, the company said. Fractional shares will be paid in cash, Computer Learning said.</p>
<p>After the split, the number of outstanding shares of Computer Learning's common stock will increase to approximately 7.8 million, the company said.</p>
</text>
